// review-panel-run.bml — ask the installed reviewer CLIs to read an artifact and answer one question, in parallel, and collect their
// answers as files. Outside review stops being an event and becomes a habit: one door.
//
//   printf '{"artifact":"docs/x.md","question":"what here is unsupported?"}' | ./fkwu observe/review-panel-run.bml
//   printf '{"artifact":"a.md","question":"..","panel":"grok,claude"}'        | ./fkwu observe/review-panel-run.bml
//   printf '{"list":1}'                                                        | ./fkwu observe/review-panel-run.bml
//
// stdin is one JSON object: artifact (a file), question, panel (doors separated by commas; the default is grok,claude,codex,cursor),
// deadline_s (a reviewer's wall time, 1800), list (1 names the doors and their state and runs nothing). Answers land in
// <temp>/review-panel/<time>/<door>.out (stderr in .err, the exit in .rc) and their paths are printed, then one line per door:
// DOOR RC BYTES FIRST-LINE. Nothing is written into the repo.
//
// A request that does not read is refused by name with exit 1 (door-options.bml): malformed JSON, an unknown key, a key of the wrong kind,
// and a panel naming a door the table below does not hold (a name that merely stands on PATH is never begun).
//
// THE DOORS, as measured 2026-07-28 on this host (a reviewer is a rented program: the body begins it by argv and reads its answer as a file)
//   grok     grok -p "<prompt>"                             open
//   claude   claude -p "<prompt>"                           open
//   codex    codex exec --skip-git-repo-check "<prompt>"    open (needs >=0.145.0)
//   cursor   cursor-agent -p --trust "<prompt>"             open (--trust, never --force or --yolo: the panel reads and opines, it never executes)
//   gemini   no headless door on this host (the CLI is tier-refused, Antigravity ships none): kept as a door that is CLOSED, so its absence stays visible
// ISOLATION: each reviewer runs from an empty scratch directory holding only a copy of the artifact (`env -C`), never from the repo; the
// artifact's text is embedded in the prompt, so a reviewer needs no filesystem reach. A reviewer past its deadline is ended with its lineage.
// The panel itself is form-stdlib/bml/review-panel.bml; its band is observe/tests/review-panel-band.bml.
// preflight-exec: forbidden
// preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/bml/stdin-source.bml form-stdlib/bml/review-panel.bml
section [form.bml] {
 let doc = rpr-doc(stdin-text());
 let ran = rpr-int(doc, "list", 0) == 1 ? rpr-list() : rpr-run(doc);
 0;
}
